WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.840
How fast can one living cell destroy a protein?

2
00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.340
Chapter 1 ended with the brake lifting.

3
00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:11.480
The APC/C tagged securin, and the proteasome destroyed it.

4
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.160
Now, how can you read that speed?

5
00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:21.857
Tag securin with a fluorescent protein, and film a single cell.

6
00:00:23.157 --> 00:00:25.237
The glow tracks how much securin is left.

7
00:00:26.537 --> 00:00:31.397
In human HeLa cells, it starts to fall at metaphase, once the checkpoint is

8
00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:32.397
satisfied.

9
00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:35.370
Here are made-up numbers, for practice.

10
00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:39.800
At metaphase, 100 percent.

11
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:41.630
Five minutes later, 71.

12
00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:46.690
Ten minutes, 50. Fifteen minutes, 35.

13
00:00:47.933 --> 00:00:51.893
Treat this as exponential loss, with no new securin made.

14
00:00:53.113 --> 00:00:54.513
At 10 minutes, half is gone.

15
00:00:55.793 --> 00:00:57.073
That time is the half-life.

16
00:00:58.353 --> 00:01:02.013
For exponential loss, a half-life removes half of what remains.

17
00:01:03.373 --> 00:01:06.193
The loss is a steady fraction, not a steady amount.

18
00:01:07.283 --> 00:01:08.963
Here is a test for you.

19
00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:12.763
Ten minutes took the glow from 100 down to 50.

20
00:01:14.103 --> 00:01:15.523
What will it read at 20 minutes?

21
00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:23.610
25 percent, not zero.

22
00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:26.250
Two half-lives halve it twice.

23
00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:32.090
The first 10 minutes lost 50 points; the next 10 lost only 25.

24
00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:34.620
The curve has a formula.

25
00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:39.360
f of t equals f zero times e to the minus k t.

26
00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:45.160
The rate constant k is ln 2 divided by the half-life.

27
00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:49.600
Here, k is about 0.069 per minute.

28
00:01:50.683 --> 00:01:54.223
Each securin the proteasome destroys is gone for good.

29
00:01:55.323 --> 00:01:57.803
While none is made, the curve can only fall.

30
00:01:59.083 --> 00:02:02.923
That fall is the one-way step from chapter 1, measured in minutes.

31
00:02:03.967 --> 00:02:07.747
So read this exponential destruction curve by its half-life.

32
00:02:09.107 --> 00:02:11.027
Every half-life halves what is left.

33
00:02:12.287 --> 00:02:16.167
From that one number you get the rate, and predict when any level is reached.
